# Pendulum octocopter — SITL tuning (load every boot)
#   In MAVProxy:  param load pendulum.parm
#   Or at launch: sim_vehicle.py ... --add-param-file=pendulum.parm
#
# BOOT / ARM SEQUENCE (these are timing, NOT params — don't try to skip them):
#   1. param load pendulum.parm
#   2. WAIT ~20-30s: until "Main loop slow" stops AND GPS locks.
#      ("Need Position Estimate" just means GPS hasn't locked yet — LOITER
#       needs a position fix by definition; you cannot param it away.)
#   3. rc 3 1000          (throttle down, or "Throttle too high")
#   4. mode LOITER        (or arm in ALT_HOLD first, switch to LOITER airborne)
#   5. arm throttle
#   6. rc 3 1500          (mid = hold alt; roll/pitch centered = hold position)
#
# --- bridge / timing ---
# All three physics clocks MUST agree or lockstep reports "Main loop slow":
#   Godot common/physics_ticks_per_second (project.godot) == SCHED_LOOP_RATE == SIM_RATE_HZ
# SIM_RATE_HZ defaults to 1200 (built-in copter physics); with the external Godot
# JSON backend delivering frames at 200 Hz, that 6x mismatch makes lockstep think
# the backend is perpetually behind and the achieved loop rate collapses to ~150 Hz
# (logged as "PreArm: Main loop slow (151Hz < 200Hz)" -> can't arm). Match it to Godot.
SCHED_LOOP_RATE 200
SIM_RATE_HZ 200
# --- arming: skip INS check (gyro rate unsatisfiable in JSON lockstep; bit4=16) ---
ARMING_SKIPCHK 16
# --- auto-disarm: 0 = never auto-disarm (default 10s after it thinks it landed).
#     Stops the motors dropping out while you fiddle on the ground / between tests. ---
DISARM_DELAY 0
# --- motor thrust model: match the sim's LINEAR thrust ---
#   Hover throttle MEASURED from CTUN.ThO at steady hover (log 43) = 0.069, NOT 0.10
#   (~1100 PWM = 0.069 thr after MOT_SPIN_MIN scaling; the old "0.10" was a bad
#   PWM->throttle conversion). pos_control's integrator made 0.10 work anyway, but
#   0.069 is correct and reduces the alt-hold trim error.
MOT_SPIN_ARM 0.03
MOT_SPIN_MIN 0.05
MOT_THST_EXPO 0.35
MOT_THST_HOVER 0.069
# --- rate loop: airframe is ~10x twitchier than default copter (low inertia, 10:1 T/W) ---
ATC_RAT_RLL_P 0.015
ATC_RAT_RLL_I 0.015
ATC_RAT_RLL_D 0.001
ATC_RAT_PIT_P 0.015
ATC_RAT_PIT_I 0.015
ATC_RAT_PIT_D 0.001
# yaw was left at stock (0.18 = 12x roll/pitch) -> canted motors (the yaw actuator)
# slammed full-range 1050<->1950 at 2Hz once the motor lag added phase delay. Cut ~9x.
ATC_RAT_YAW_P 0.02
ATC_RAT_YAW_I 0.002
ATC_RAT_YAW_D 0.0
# --- vertical loop: same 10x-too-hot problem as attitude. Throttle->accel gain
#     is ~96 m/s^2 (10:1 T/W) so stock PSC_D_ACC_P=0.05 gives loop gain ~4.8 ->
#     bang-bang limit cycle (throttle slams 0<->0.14). Cut accel gains ~10x. ---
PSC_D_ACC_P 0.005
PSC_D_ACC_I 0.02
# NOTE: vertical felt laggy mainly because of PILOT_ACC_Z (default 2.5 m/s^2 clamps how
# fast the alt controller builds climb accel) + PSC_JERK_D. To make climb snappier raise
# them (e.g. PILOT_ACC_Z 10-15, PSC_JERK_D 30) -- left at defaults here for the baseline.
# stop hover-throttle mis-learning off the limit cycle during tuning (0=disabled)
MOT_HOVER_LEARN 0
# --- LOITER feel for manual keyboard control (NOT comms latency) ---
#   LOIT_BRK_DELAY 1.0 = it COASTS for a full second after you release a key
#     before braking -> the "keeps going then settles later". Set 0.
#   LOIT_SPEED 12.5 m/s is race-pace; drop to 3 so a key tap is gentle.
#   Brake harder/snappier so it stops promptly when you let go.
LOIT_BRK_DELAY 0
LOIT_SPEED_MS 3.0
LOIT_BRK_ACC_M 5.0
LOIT_BRK_JRK_M 10.0
# --- rig controller (rig_controller.lua, GUIDED): open the kinematic limits so
#     lateral dart is real. GUIDED posvelaccel targets are gated by the WP_* nav
#     params (confirmed in mode_guided.cpp: horizontal WP_SPD/WP_ACC, vertical
#     WP_SPD_UP/WP_SPD_DN/WP_ACC_Z). They default WAY below this airframe's
#     ~48 m/s^2 lateral capacity. Start modest and raise once it tracks cleanly;
#     the cap is the controller's, not the airframe's.
#
#   NOTE — this build renamed/SI-converted WPNav: prefix is WP_ (not WPNAV_) and
#   values are SI (m/s, m/s^2), NOT cm. The old WPNAV_SPEED 500 etc. would load
#   as UNKNOWN PARAMS and silently leave GUIDED clamped at defaults.
#
#   Must exceed MAX_LAT_VEL (4.0) / MAX_VERT_VEL (1.5) in the script. WP_ACC's
#   advisory @Range tops at 5 but param set isn't clamped — 12 is accepted.
#   (NOTE: this loader rejects inline comments — keep value lines bare.)
#   WP_SPD   horiz speed cap, m/s    (> MAX_LAT_VEL 4.0)
#   WP_ACC   horiz accel cap, m/s^2  (airframe can do ~48; raise later)
#   WP_JERK  horiz jerk, m/s^3       (smoothness vs snap)
#   WP_SPD_UP/DN  vertical speed caps, m/s  (> MAX_VERT_VEL 1.5)
#   WP_ACC_Z vertical accel cap, m/s^2  (momentary up/down headroom) ---
WP_SPD 5
WP_ACC 12
WP_JERK 20
WP_SPD_UP 2.5
WP_SPD_DN 2.5
WP_ACC_Z 5
